      "id": "M06C1-P2-001",
      "priority": "P2",
      "title": "Compare declared presence as content membership",
      "path": "crates/vibe-orchestrator/src/machine_operation/boot_debugger/dispatch.rs",
      "line": 188,
      "end_line": 213,
      "cause": "Both maps include every declared resource path, including raw-absent resources whose digest is None. Same host declarations are fixed. Therefore added/removed vectors cannot describe normal create/delete/move; those transitions are mislabeled changed.",
      "scenario": "Declare b.md while absent. Freeze old. Registered client Create b.md then freeze and retain_capture. Both maps contain b.md, None versus Some(hash): added=[],changed=[b.md]. Delete reverses it but removed stays empty. Move produces two changed paths rather than removed source+added destination.",
      "requirement": "M06C1 current compare models on actual M16 overlay/capture contract must report truthful immutable snapshot differences; no unavailable stub or made-up success.",
      "minimal_fix": "Use captured active presence/raw availability when building content-membership maps, distinguish explicit absent versus unavailable if necessary; changed only when present in both with different digest. Preserve old snapshots.",
      "minimal_regression": "One actual registered-client overlay test exercising absent\u2192Create and Delete/Move, passed through retain_capture and public Compare. Assert added/removed/changed exact lists and old inspect result unchanged."
    },
    {
      "id": "M06C1-P2-002",
      "priority": "P2",
      "title": "Preserve captured source/position mapping in the debugger result",
      "path": "crates/vibe-orchestrator/src/machine_operation/boot_debugger.rs",
      "line": 213,
      "end_line": 227,
      "cause": "Projection maps GraphOccurrence to Node but drops artifact_lines and emits a numeric graph source index without the graph source identity catalogue. Resources describe host document resources, a different index space. Explain returns only occurrence indices; page rows contain opaque reference IDs, so available positions cannot be recovered structurally.",
      "scenario": "A committed STATIC artifact containing a closed nested embed marker has a B1 occurrence with exact artifact_lines(start,end), source identity and known parent. Inspect returns parent/requested but no range/basis mapping. If host admits vibe.toml and STATIC.md, graph source0 does not mean host resource0; consumer must guess or reparse raw bytes.",
      "requirement": "M06C1 step3 source-position basis plus existing PROP072 CAPTURED-GRAPH preserving every available position and source identity. Existing raw chunk access does not substitute for structured captured coordinates.",
      "minimal_fix": "Carry existing captured source identities and optional recorded artifact ranges into the registered result, bound to artifact resource+snapshot and explicit basis. Retain absence/unavailable when no mapping was captured. Use existing mappings only; no new parser, invented authored span or ancestry.",
      "coordinate_meaning": "artifact_lines are one-based lines of the captured emitted artifact, not authored source lines. Bind to exact artifact resource/digest/snapshot; only provide raw-byte/editor offsets if incumbent owner can map them. SourceDoc/source-position mappings keep their own captured basis and identity.",
      "minimal_regression": "Inspect a real static marker capture with nested embed through shared route; assert exact source join and captured emitted line range+basis. Separate unmapped carrier asserts typed unavailable, never0/fabricated authored coordinate; old snapshot result remains stable after live-file change."
    }
  ],
